      "title": "Australian politics live: Opposition hammers Labor over $150m ‘Cop flop’; Tehan kicked out of parliament for ‘taking mickey’ with Molly Meldrum catchphrase",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/nov/23/anthony-albanese-digital-duty-of-care-labor-greens-coalition-one-nation-angus-taylor-pauline-hanson-penny-wong-ai-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>‘Very difficult to bridge that divide’: Murray Watt</strong></p><p>Cabinet minister <strong>Murray Watt</strong> says it’s increasingly difficult to bridge the divide between nations on climate policy after a frustrating Cop summit that didn’t reach a final agreement.</p><p>It’s obviously a very deeply disappointing outcome that the cover decision was not agreed to by all nations.</p><p>I think what this shows is a very challenging international environment at the moment to reach agreement on almost anything and particularly a situation like this where you’ve got fossil fuel producers on the one hand and other countries that are experiencing very serious impacts from climate change.</p><p>We’re seeing much greater defence engagement between Australia and Japan, Australia and the Philippines, and the Philippines and Japan.</p><p>Even though I think it doesn’t quite come across in its overall score, that US defence relationship in the region is stronger, which is helping Australia.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/nov/23/anthony-albanese-digital-duty-of-care-labor-greens-coalition-one-nation-angus-taylor-pauline-hanson-penny-wong-ai-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-23T04:19:17"
    },
    {
      "title": "Doula thought self-described birth keeper was clinically trained before NSW baby death, inquest hears",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/23/doula-thought-self-described-birth-keeper-was-clinically-trained-before-nsw-baby-death-inquest-hears-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Inquest into the deaths of four babies after free and home births hears doula urged client to attend birth centre</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/nov/23/anthony-albanese-digital-duty-of-care-labor-greens-coalition-one-nation-angus-taylor-pauline-hanson-penny-wong-ai-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia politics live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A doula who supported a free birth without any medical professionals present has told an inquest that she thought a self-described birth keeper who was assisting her was clinically trained.</p><p>The child, known in court as Baby R, died after the free birth. Baby R’s death is one of four being examined in a joint coronial inquest in Lismore, which has heard that three babies died after being born in free births, and a fourth during a home birth between 2022 and 2024.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/23/doula-thought-self-described-birth-keeper-was-clinically-trained-before-nsw-baby-death-inquest-hears-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-23T04:03:07"
    },
    {
      "title": "Beau Lamarre-Condon acted like a ‘poorly behaved boyfriend’ before alleged double murders, defence argues",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/23/beau-lamarre-condon-trail-executed-jesse-baird-prosecution-argues-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Crown says accused developed ‘jealous obsession’ but defence says ‘love makes fools of us’ </p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/nov/23/anthony-albanese-digital-duty-of-care-labor-greens-coalition-one-nation-angus-taylor-pauline-hanson-penny-wong-ai-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia politics live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Beau Lamarre-Condon acted like a “poorly behaved boyfriend” before allegedly murdering Jesse Baird and Luke Davies, a court has heard.</p><p>Lamarre-Condon is accused of fatally shooting the Sydney couple with his police service weapon in Baird’s Paddington home on 19 February 2024.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/23/beau-lamarre-condon-trail-executed-jesse-baird-prosecution-argues-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
